{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>For a lamp</b> — For the commandment is like a lamp to illuminate before you, as in 'the commandment of YHWH is clear, illuminating the eyes' (Psalms 19:9). And the Torah is like light to those who study it, and 'the fool walks in darkness' (Ecclesiastes 2:14), and the way of life and the wisdom to the person who receives it is a path by which he will live."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:12.710910948Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}